so i don't know about you guys but every  time i think i've explored 100 of this  game i am consistently surprised by the  amount of content that i just seem to  miss i've beaten this game four times  now all with at least 50 hours of play  time between them and i just now found  the entrance to reichard's divine tower  where you can receive his great room now  most of you guys are smarter and better  than i am at these games but i've really  tried to avoid looking up how to do  things in elden ring and for the longest  time i just couldn't find the entrance  to this divine tower i even went inside  this cave multiple times and just  thought it was a very basic cave that  had nothing in it my original thought  was that i had to find a teleporter that  would take me to the tower just like i  had to do for the isolated tower but  during my fifth playthrough i decided to  give it another try basically it really  did seem like the only possible route to  the divine tower it's the closest cave  system to the tower itself the cave is  also named the sealed tunnel which  indicated that something is obviously  being sealed away and after exploring  more of the cave there are multiple  invisible walls which has been a major  rarity in elden ring compared to dark  souls there are actually three or four  invisible walls in this tunnel alone and  it leads to some very interesting areas  that i'd like to lure hunt through with  you guys today making my way through the  sealed tunnel brought up a lot of  questions for me like what are they  mining in this area are they looking for  the same invisible walls that i had to  find are they the ones that sealed it  away in the first place these mining  enemy npcs do seem to be infatuated with  the meteoric elements that are spread  around in the lands between like they'll  constantly be mining in caves where  there are crystals or other meteoric  elements and exploring further into this  cave we find an onyx lord and upon  defeating this boss we receive his  greatsword that reads a weapon unique to  the onyx lords a race of ancients with  the skin of stone who was said to have  risen to life when a meteor struck long  ago that's likely what this meteor on  the map is i've always been so curious  of why this is here we also know that  these onyx lords are at least one of  them who went on to be the sorcerer  master and radon's teacher but that  doesn't mean there's only one onyx lord  there's probably multiple of them so  either the entrance to reichard's divine  tower was sealed away by the capital  city and the golden order or the onyx  lord sealed himself and the tower away i  say that maybe the capital city and the  golden order sealed away this divine  tower because the story of reichard is  embarrassing to the lineage of the  golden order itself as reichardt is one  of the demigod children of ratagon and  rinala again reichard would be  considered a demigod's stepchild since  ratagon would go on to be queen  america's consort reichardt is an  embarrassment since he decided to feed  himself to the great serpent for reasons  that i have not found yet his great rune  reads reichard was amongst the children  of ranala and radagon who became demigod  stepchildren of ratagon's union with  queen america reichardt fed himself to  the blasphemous serpent great rune and  all so clearly reichardt didn't care  much for the responsibilities that came  with obtaining the power of a great room  or maybe he just didn't want to be a  part of the war between all his brothers  sisters and step siblings i'm curious of  what you guys all think may have been  the reason reichardt decided to be  consumed by the great rune serpent maybe  it was just to obtain more power which  is my best guess he doesn't really seem  to be liked by anybody in his family but  as i said i feel the family lineage was  stained by reichardt's decision and they  sealed this divine tower away so none  could bear witness or even remember his  existence it also probably has a lot to  do with the volcano manor whose entire  point is to be rid of the golden order  itself maybe he did it all just despite  his family who knows it's funny to me  that all these demigods and the family  would just disregard morgot and banish  him to the sewers below of the capital  city just because he was born as an omen  morgot was clearly the most loyal to the  family its lineage and its reputation  definitely more so than reichardt and  godric who if you guys didn't know this  godric does not seem to be a child of  america and ratagon or at least that's  what i can read from his great rune i  didn't know that till today which is  very interesting so it seems like godric  just stole godwin's great rune and then  just went crazy with the grafting  process nobody in the family line seems  to like godric whatsoever but it's  interesting to see that he's not  actually a descendant he was just  powerful enough being godwin's offspring  that he could obtain the power of a  great rune and then it seems like he  just disregards his father's body down  to the bottom of stornville castle this  is such an interesting thing to look  into that we will look into more and who  knows maybe it was morgot who sealed  away the entrance to reichard's divine  tower he's clearly not happy with all  his siblings and their fickleness to the  golden order itself we've all heard how  he feels  ah  godric the golden  the twin prodigies  michela and melania  general pradhan  prata reichardt  luna princess ronnie  willful traitors  this guy was banished as an omen and  still remains so devout to the cause of  his family's line his story really is a  sad one and so is all of elden rings in  my opinion it's very clear that this  tower was sealed away or at least the  tunnel was sealed away so that nobody  could find it and when we scale  reichard's divine tower we get the best  view of the other divine towers in the  lands between we can see all of them and  if you didn't notice this before these  divine towers are placed in a circle  meant to represent a ring putting all  the great runes together would make the  elden ring so it's cool they're placed  in a ring themselves i always wondered  if it was in a literal sense that queen  america shattered the elden ring maybe  she destroyed one of the divine towers  that we just simply don't know about to  technically destroy the elden ring  because we've been to all the divine  towers except for mykolas we have yet to  find his great room we can receive a  great rune from godric melania radon  morgot reichard and moogue but still no  sign of nicolas very interesting we'll  likely have to wait for future dlc to  learn more about mykola which i'm very  excited about i've seen some theories on  twitter that we'll be able to access  future dlc by touching nikola's hand and  he'll teleport us through time or  something like that it's almost like the  world of elden ring is set up to have  future content added to it for years to  come it's all very exciting i can't wait  thank you guys for watching the video  and continuing to support this channel  make sure to like subscribe and join our  discord community so we can discuss more  things of the world of elden ring take  care and i'll see you all in the next  video  [Music]  you
 

